<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Hui Shung to tender for 54,000T soy/corn.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Hui Shung to tender for 54,000T soy/corn.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Hui Shung Group will tender on Thursday for a shipment comprising 46,000 tonnes of soybeans and 8,000 tonnes of corn originating in the United States or South America, traders said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p>			   U.S. Gulf	Pacific N.W.</p>
<p> Corn	 8,000    Aug 21-Sept 5  Sept 6-20</p>
<p> Soybean   46,000    Aug 21-Sept 5  Sept 6-20</p>
<p>-- or --</p>
<p> Type	Tonne     Date/Location</p>
<p>			   Brazil/Argentine port</p>
<p> Corn	 8,000    Aug 21 - Sept 10</p>
<p> Soybean   46,000    Aug 21 - Sept 10</p>
<p>The Hui Shung Group includes Hui Shung Agriculture and Food Corp, Eagle Food Industry and Charoen Pokphand.</p>
<p>-- George Hsu, Taipei newsroom (8862-5080815)</p>
